# Backend API Development Standards

## **MANDATORY: API Development Patterns**

### **Reference Implementation**

Use [backend/auth-service/](mdc:backend/auth-service/) as the complete reference for all new backend services.

### **Standard Response Format**

```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT: Success response
{
  "status": "success",
  "message": "Operation completed successfully",
  "data": { /* response data */ },
  "meta": {
    "timestamp": "2024-01-15T10:30:00.000Z",
    "service": "user-service",
    "requestId": "req-uuid"
  }
}

// ✅ CORRECT: Error response
{
  "status": "error",
  "error": {
    "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",
    "message": "Request validation failed",
    "details": [/* validation errors */]
  },
  "meta": {
    "timestamp": "2024-01-15T10:30:00.000Z",
    "service": "user-service",
    "requestId": "req-uuid"
  }
}
```

### **Audit Logging Pattern**

```javascript
// ✅ REQUIRED: Audit all CRUD operations
const result = await prisma.$transaction(async (tx) => {
  const user = await tx.user.create({
    data: userData,
    select: { id: true, email: true, role: true },
  });

  // MANDATORY: Audit log entry
  await tx.auditLog.create({
    data: {
      userId: req.user?.id,
      action: "CREATE",
      resource: "user",
      resourceId: user.id,
      changes: userData,
      ipAddress: req.ip,
      userAgent: req.get("User-Agent"),
    },
  });

  return user;
});
```

### **Input Validation Pattern**

```javascript
// ✅ REQUIRED: Joi validation for all endpoints
const createUserSchema = Joi.object({
  email: Joi.string().email().required(),
  name: Joi.string().min(2).max(100).required(),
  role: Joi.string()
    .valid("admin", "finance", "operations", "client", "support")
    .default("client"),
});

// Usage in routes
router.post(
  "/users",
  authenticateToken,
  validate(createUserSchema),
  UserController.createUser
);
```

## **Authentication & Authorization**

### **JWT Middleware Pattern**

```javascript
// middleware/auth.js - Standard pattern from auth-service
const authenticateToken = async (req, res, next) => {
  const token = req.headers.authorization?.split(" ")[1];

  if (!token) {
    return res
      .status(401)
      .json(errorResponse("MISSING_TOKEN", "Access token required"));
  }

  try {
    const decoded = jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET);
    req.user = decoded;
    next();
  } catch (error) {
    return res
      .status(403)
      .json(errorResponse("INVALID_TOKEN", "Invalid token"));
  }
};
```

### **Role-Based Access Control**

```javascript
// Follow auth-service RBAC pattern
const requireRole = (allowedRoles) => {
  return (req, res, next) => {
    if (!allowedRoles.includes(req.user.role)) {
      return res
        .status(403)
        .json(errorResponse("INSUFFICIENT_PERMISSIONS", "Access denied"));
    }
    next();
  };
};
```

## **Database Operations**

### **MANDATORY: Prisma Transactions**

```javascript
// ✅ REQUIRED: Use transactions for multi-table operations
const updateUserWithAudit = async (userId, updateData, req) => {
  return await prisma.$transaction(async (tx) => {
    const user = await tx.user.update({
      where: { id: userId },
      data: updateData,
    });

    await tx.auditLog.create({
      data: {
        userId: req.user.id,
        action: "UPDATE",
        resource: "user",
        resourceId: userId,
        changes: updateData,
        ipAddress: req.ip,
        userAgent: req.get("User-Agent"),
      },
    });

    return user;
  });
};
```

### **Standard Prisma Schema Pattern**

```prisma
// Every service MUST include audit logging
model AuditLog {
  id         String   @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  userId     String?  @map("user_id") @db.Uuid
  action     String   @db.VarChar(100)
  resource   String   @db.VarChar(100)
  resourceId String?  @map("resource_id") @db.Uuid
  changes    Json?
  ipAddress  String?  @map("ip_address") @db.Inet
  userAgent  String?  @map("user_agent")
  createdAt  DateTime @default(now()) @map("created_at")

  @@index([userId])
  @@index([createdAt])
  @@index([resource])
  @@map("audit_logs")
}
```

## **Error Handling**

### **Custom Error Classes**

```javascript
// shared/lib/errors.js - Use existing patterns
class ValidationError extends Error {
  constructor(message, details = null) {
    super(message);
    this.name = "ValidationError";
    this.statusCode = 400;
    this.code = "VALIDATION_ERROR";
    this.details = details;
  }
}

class NotFoundError extends Error {
  constructor(resource, id) {
    super(`${resource} with ID ${id} not found`);
    this.name = "NotFoundError";
    this.statusCode = 404;
    this.code = "NOT_FOUND";
  }
}
```

