## **Service Implementation Checklist**

### **MANDATORY: Every Service Must Have**

- [ ] Prisma schema with audit logging models
- [ ] JWT authentication middleware
- [ ] Input validation with Joi schemas
- [ ] Standard response format helpers
- [ ] Error handling middleware
- [ ] Audit logging for all CRUD operations
- [ ] Health check endpoint
- [ ] Swagger API documentation

### **File Structure Pattern**

```
service-name/
├── controllers/     # Business logic with Prisma
├── middleware/      # Auth, validation, error handling
├── routes/         # API endpoints with Swagger docs
├── validation/     # Joi validation schemas
├── prisma/         # Schema and migrations
├── config/         # Database configuration
└── server.js       # Express app setup
```

## **CRITICAL: Controller Pattern Enforcement**

### **MANDATORY: No Inline Functions in Routes**

**ALL business logic MUST be in controller methods - NEVER use inline functions in routes.**

```javascript
// ❌ FORBIDDEN: Inline functions in routes
router.get("/users/:id", auth.authenticate, async (req, res) => {
  try {
    const user = await prisma.user.findUnique({
      where: { id: req.params.id },
    });
    // 20+ lines of business logic here - WRONG!
    res.json({ user });
  } catch (error) {
    // Error handling here - WRONG!
  }
});

// ✅ CORRECT: Proper controller method
router.get("/users/:id", auth.authenticate, asyncHandler(UserController.getUser));

// Controller implementation
class UserController {
  static async getUser(req, res) {
    try {
      const { id } = req.params;
      
      const user = await prisma.user.findUnique({
        where: { id },
        select: { id: true, email: true, role: true },
      });

      if (!user) {
        throw new NotFoundError("User", id);
      }

      // Audit logging
      await prisma.auditLog.create({
        data: {
          userId: req.user.userId,
          action: "GET_USER",
          resource: "User",
          resourceId: id,
          ipAddress: req.ip,
          userAgent: req.get("User-Agent"),
        },
      });

      res.json(APIResponse.success({ user }));
    } catch (error) {
      logger.error("Get user error", {
        error: error.message,
        userId: req.params.id,
        service: "user-service",
      });
      throw error;
    }
  }
}
```

### **Controller Method Requirements**

Every controller method MUST include:

- ✅ **Static Methods**: All controller methods must be static
- ✅ **Error Handling**: Comprehensive try/catch with proper error logging
- ✅ **Audit Logging**: All CRUD operations must create audit logs
- ✅ **Input Validation**: Parameter and body validation (handled by middleware)
- ✅ **Structured Responses**: Use APIResponse.success() and APIResponse.error()
- ✅ **Logging**: Detailed logging for debugging and monitoring
- ✅ **Prisma Transactions**: Use transactions for multi-table operations

### **Route Organization Pattern**

```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT: Clean route definitions
const express = require("express");
const { asyncHandler } = require("../middleware/errorHandler");
const auth = require("../middleware/auth");
const { validateCreateUser, validateUuidParam } = require("../middleware/validate");
const UserController = require("../controllers/userController");

const router = express.Router();

// All routes use controller methods - NO inline functions
router.post("/users", auth.adminOnly, validateCreateUser, asyncHandler(UserController.createUser));
router.get("/users", auth.authenticate, asyncHandler(UserController.listUsers));
router.get("/users/:id", auth.authenticate, validateUuidParam, asyncHandler(UserController.getUser));
router.put("/users/:id", auth.authenticate, validateUuidParam, asyncHandler(UserController.updateUser));
router.delete("/users/:id", auth.adminOnly, validateUuidParam, asyncHandler(UserController.deleteUser));

module.exports = router;
```

## **NEVER DO**

- ❌ **Use inline functions in routes** (ALL logic must be in controllers)
- ❌ Write raw SQL queries (use Prisma only)
- ❌ Skip audit logging for CRUD operations
- ❌ Create endpoints without authentication
- ❌ Skip input validation
- ❌ Use custom response formats
- ❌ Skip error handling middleware
- ❌ Create services without health checks
- ❌ Put business logic directly in route handlers
